        "record_index": 5745,
        "record_sha256": "64a84ed86708387bc636eb6e0d2d1c097f84f8bd1a442361eb9a1ead8404b5c9",
        "speaker": "Astra",
        "text": "Astra: You began inspecting the arrays, then moved to missing-data techniques without establishing that filling X serves this example. Leave X unresolved for now. Look instead at your sentence saying 36.24 appears in both sequences: does the displayed text support that sentence? In English, revise only that claim to match what you can inspect. How much checking is enough for this textual correction, and what additional evidence would be needed before calling it a change in real measurements?"
